# tools/ales_stereo_reverb_gate_env_witness.rish — the stereo envelope gate: the reverb's GATED TAIL given a shaped edge, across a stereo master (ALES203).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES203.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-111333_fill-ales203-lotus-stereo-reverb-gate-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye (ALES191 — the named-room stereo wet, run over the master unchanged); lotus/gate_env.rye (ALES54 — the
# attack/release envelope gate and its guards, run per channel); lotus/reverb_gate_env.rye (ALES202 — the mono envelope gate this mirrors per ear);
# lotus/stereo_reverb_gate.rye (ALES201 — the static stereo gate this contains as its instantaneous limit); lotus/pan.rye (the StereoClip);
# lotus/clock.rye (ALES5 — the sample clock); lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip each channel holds, its sample_max the gate's rail).
#
# lotus/stereo_reverb_gate_env.rye carries ALES202's shaped-edge gated tail across a stereo master — the SAME time-following envelope gate over BOTH
# channels of a StereoClip, one shared threshold, ratio, and attack/release, the image held. It reverberates the master wet in place through ALES191's
# stereo_reverb_preset UNCHANGED, prechecks the threshold, ratio, and both coefficients (the SAME guards ALES54 raises) BEFORE the wet is written so a
# bad gate leaves both channels DRY and balanced (atomic), then follow-gates each channel's wet with a fresh envelope and no cross-channel read — the
# left ear follow-gates left, the right ear follow-gates right, so the image the preset held is held. It invents no new audio arithmetic. The selftest
# proves on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a firm ratio each channel equals
# stereo_reverb_preset then gate_follow on that channel byte for byte and each shaped-gated channel differs from its wet; with unit attack and unit
# release it equals ALES201's static stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte (the static gate is its zero-smoothing limit); each gated channel's total energy
# is strictly less than its wet's; the image is held (a centred master identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master distinct); the channels leave
# balanced and silence stays silence; and the faults forward atomic (a bad threshold BadThreshold, a bad ratio BadRatio, an illegal coefficient
# BadCoeff with both channels still dry, DurationTooLong, BadRange). Purely local — one StereoClip, a validated clock; no network, no keys, no funds,
# no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_reverb_gate_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Language EN — ALES202 gave the MONO reverb its shaped-edge gated tail (a time-following envelope gate whose release holds the gate open over the decay, so the tail breathes rather than chops); a keeper mixing a STEREO master still had only the STATIC stereo gate (ALES201), the shaped edge stopped at mono exactly as the static gate did before ALES201 carried it across. This rung is the thin twin ALES202 named next: the SAME envelope gate, over BOTH channels of a StereoClip, one shared threshold, ratio, and attack/release, the image held — a clean composition of ALES191's stereo wet and ALES54's proven envelope gate run per ear."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Style Radiant — the identity edge is stated positively and proven exact on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte (a unit-ratio follow-gate is the un-gated stereo reverb); a larger ratio cuts the below-threshold tail harder on both ears, and a slower release holds the gate open longer over each ear's decay. The static stereo gate (ALES201) lives on as this rung's zero-smoothing limit: unit attack and unit release make each envelope the bare magnitude, so stereo_reverb_gate_env then equals stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte on both channels. The image is held — the left ear follow-gates left, the right ear follow-gates right, with a fresh envelope per ear and no cross-channel read."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: Lens TAME — one StereoClip of i16 PCM, a validated clock, and ALES191's fixed banks; NO new audio arithmetic — the gate is ALES54's proven envelope-following gate over the proven stereo wet, run per ear; StereoReverbGateEnvError = stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || BadThreshold || BadRatio || BadCoeff, the gate's threshold, ratio, and both coefficients PRECHECKED before the wet is written (the same guards ALES54 raises) so a bad gate leaves both channels dry and balanced (atomic), DurationTooLong / BadRange / BadThreshold / BadRatio / BadCoeff by name before any write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device. A wet-tail stereo envelope gate; the attack/release are fractions per sample index."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_gate_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env line"

# This rung runs ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset over its public API for the wet — re-prove the stereo named-room preset still stands green beside it.
let preset = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-preset' && echo yes"]
assert (trim preset.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the ALES191 stereo named-room preset regressed under its envelope gate"

# And re-prove ALES202's mono envelope gate still stands green — the rung this mirrors per ear.
let monoenv = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/reverb_gate_env.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/reverb_gate_env && lotus/bin/reverb_gate_env selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb-gate-env' && echo yes"]
assert (trim monoenv.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the ALES202 mono envelope gate regressed beside its stereo twin"

# And re-prove ALES201's static stereo gate still stands green — the instantaneous limit this rung equals.
let staticgate = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_gate.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_gate selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-gate' && echo yes"]
assert (trim staticgate.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: the ALES201 static stereo gate regressed beside its envelope gate"

say "ales-stereo-reverb-gate-env: GREEN — the stereo envelope gate: the reverb's GATED TAIL given a shaped edge, across a stereo master. Reverberate the master wet in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, then follow-gate each channel's wet with ALES54's proven envelope gate at the same threshold, ratio, and attack/release — run per ear with a fresh envelope and no cross-channel read, ratio_num == ratio_den the identity, a larger ratio cutting the quiet tail harder, a slower release holding the gate open longer — no new audio arithmetic. Proven on both channels: at ratio_num == ratio_den exactly stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a firm ratio each channel equals stereo_reverb_preset then gate_follow byte for byte and each shaped-gated channel differs from its wet; with unit attack and unit release it equals ALES201's static stereo_reverb_gate byte for byte; each gated channel's total energy is strictly less than its wet's; the image is held (a centred master identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master distinct); the channels leave balanced and silence stays silence; a bad threshold refuses BadThreshold, a bad ratio BadRatio, an illegal coefficient BadCoeff with both channels still dry, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving both channels untouched; the ALES191 stereo preset, the ALES202 mono envelope gate, and the ALES201 static stereo gate stay GREEN beside it. The gate axis now stands whole for mono and stereo in both its static and shaped forms; a fresh reverb axis (width, freeze, or early/late balance) is next."
